 * loading strategy. Each call returns its own instance with its own state, so
 * multiple sites can be handled independently (this is NOT a shared singleton).
 *
 * The eager strategy reads the whole Git repository history once (including
 * submodules) so that the first/last update info of any file can be retrieved
 * efficiently later on.
